<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galawdewos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">killed 1559</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Gelawdewos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galawdewos was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in the mid-sixteenth century, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dawit-ii">Dawit II</a>. With Portuguese help he defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Ahmad ibn Ibrahim</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wayna-daga">Wayna Daga</a> in 1543 and restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. He was killed in 1559 fighting against Adal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galawdewos.jpg" alt="Galawdewos" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mary Evans Picture Library · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claudius,_King_of_Ethiopia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
